  "chapterId": "ch1-powers-of-ten",
  "minutes": 9,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "When multiplying powers of ten, ADD the exponents: 10ᵃ × 10ᵇ = 10ᵃ⁺ᵇ. Why? 10² × 10³ means (100)×(1,000) = 100,000 = 10⁵, and 2+3=5 — every extra zero from one factor just tacks onto the other.",
      "figure": "esn-exponent-rules"
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Apply the product rule.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "10⁴ × 10³ = 10^____ (just the exponent)",
        "answer": 7,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 12,
            "feedback": "That multiplies the exponents (4×3) instead of adding them — the rule is 10ᵃ×10ᵇ=10ᵃ⁺ᵇ, so 4+3=7."
          },
          {
            "value": 1,
            "feedback": "That subtracts instead of adds — multiplying powers of ten means the exponents ADD: 4+3=7."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "10⁴ × 10³ = 10^(4+3) = 10⁷."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Dividing powers of ten SUBTRACTS the exponents: 10ᵃ ÷ 10ᵇ = 10ᵃ⁻ᵇ. This works for negative exponents too — subtracting a negative adds: 10³ ÷ 10⁻² = 10^(3−(−2)) = 10⁵.",
      "figure": "esn-exponent-rules"
    },
    {
      "id": "k1",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "Apply the quotient rule.",
      "conceptTag": "esn-powers-of-ten-arithmetic",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "10⁶ ÷ 10² = 10^(6−2) = 10⁴.",
        "Dividing powers of ten subtracts the exponents: 6−2=4."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "10⁶ ÷ 10² = 10^____ (just the exponent)",
        "answer": 4,
        "tolerance": 0,
        "commonErrors": [
          {
            "value": 3,
            "feedback": "That's off by one — 6−2=4, not 3."
          },
          {
            "value": 12,
            "feedback": "That multiplies the exponents instead of subtracting — dividing means SUBTRACT: 6−2=4."
          }
        ],
        "fallbackFeedback": "10⁶ ÷ 10² = 10^(6−2) = 10⁴."
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "power-ten-exponent"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Multiply with a negative exponent.",
